The pinned binaries are intact; the failure is caused by the audit execution sandbox exposing a host `/proc` while commands run in a nested PID namespace, so Lean’s `IO.appPath` cannot resolve `/proc/<inner-pid>/exe`. I’m using a narrowly scoped read-only compatibility shim that only supplies the known pinned executable path for that lookup. It does not modify the generated or candidate trees, and I’ll retain its source and diagnostics as audit evidence.
